<title>ITALY: Italy cabinet to meet on Thursday before budget.</title>
<headline>Italy cabinet to meet on Thursday before budget.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's cabinet will meet on Thursday at 0800 GMT, ahead of the government's presentation of its controversial 1997 budget to the lower house of parliament.</p>
<p>A government statement said the reiteration of a series of decrees including defense co-operation between Italy and Albania, a railway accord with Slovenia and an agreement on duties with Israel were on the agenda.</p>
<p>Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi is expected to present the government's 1997 budget to the Chamber of Deputies on Thursday afternoon. The package is designed to cut 62.5 trillion lire off next year's deficit and prepare Italy to join a planned single European currency from its launch in 1999.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
</text>
